Generic single-database configuration.

## Project notes

- Config file is `alembic.ini` at the repo root (`script_location = database/alembic`).
- The DB URL comes from `app.core.config.settings.database_url` (`.env`), not
  the `sqlalchemy.url` placeholder in `alembic.ini` -- `env.py` overrides it.
- Run all commands from the repo root with the project venv active
  (`source sourceme.sh`).
- New models must be imported in `src/app/models/__init__.py` before
  `--autogenerate` will see them (populates `Base.metadata`).

## Commands

```
# Create a migration from model changes (needs a reachable DB to diff against)
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short description"

# Create a blank migration to hand-write (no DB connection needed)
alembic revision -m "short description"

# Apply all pending migrations
alembic upgrade head

# Apply up to a specific revision
alembic upgrade <revision>

# Roll back the most recent migration
alembic downgrade -1

# Roll back to a specific revision, or to an empty DB
alembic downgrade <revision>
alembic downgrade base

# Show the current DB revision
alembic current

# Show full migration history
alembic history --verbose
```

Always review autogenerated migrations before applying -- Postgres extensions
(e.g. `pgvector`) and vector index types are never autogenerated and must be
added by hand with `op.execute(...)`.